      "writtenOn": "2024-01-30T20:26:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Try to understand this better, for LEA, we have\n\n- CSIP Group 1\n - Device 1-1\n   - Audio Output ID 1-1-1 (or just 1 if only locally unique within a device)\n   - Audio Output ID 1-1-2 (or just 2 if only locally unique within a device)\n - Device 1-2\n   - Audio Output ID 1-2-1 (or just 1 if only locally unique within a device)\n   - Audio Output ID 1-2-2 (or just 2 if only locally unique within a device)\n- CSIP Group 2\n - Device 2-1\n   - Audio Output ID 2-1-1 (or just 1 if only locally unique within a device)\n   - Audio Output ID 2-1-2 (or just 2 if only locally unique within a device)\n - Device 2-2\n   - Audio Output ID 2-2-1 (or just 1 if only locally unique within a device)\n   - Audio Output ID 2-2-2 (or just 2 if only locally unique within a device)\n   \nIs this the new topology we want to expose? \n\nWhat is the use case for this?\n\nIn reality, how many LE audio peripherals will really have multiple audio output IDs?",
      "revId": "907f99585fc4900b2fbda296b1704d10368c4ace",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
